<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amiternum</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amiternum was an ancient Sabine town in the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aterno-pescara">Aterno</a> valley of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, near modern L'Aquila. It came under Roman control early in the 3rd century BCE and grew into a prosperous Roman town with a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> and an amphitheatre, whose remains survive. The historian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sallust">Sallust</a> was born there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amiternum.jpg" alt="Amiternum" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lasacrasillaba · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rovine_di_Amiternum.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
